<title>UK: UK's Infobank sets AIM debut for February 18.</title>
<headline>UK's Infobank sets AIM debut for February 18.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Infobank International Holdings Plc said on Tuesday it plans to list on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) with first dealings scheduled for February 18.</p>
<p>Infobank, which has developed a system using CD-ROM and on-line services for the sale of office supplies, said it was placing shares at 125p in an issue raising over 9.0 million stg and valuing it at 24.0 million.</p>
<p>The placing is sponsored by English Trust, with Collins Stewart as broker.</p>
<p>-- John Suherland, London newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
